## Are we on track?

There's no early signal that predicts the real exam. These are leading indicators, checked at the end of each domain, with what to change if one goes red.

| Signal | How it's measured | Healthy | If not healthy, adjust by… |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Retention** | Warm-up hit rate on MissLog items reviewed 3+ days after last seen | ≥ 75% | Shorter intervals; more free-recall warm-ups; a mini review session |
| **Transfer** | Score on the 3 interleaved questions per quiz | ≥ 2/3 on average | Revisit 🟡 objectives before moving on |
| **Calibration** | Accuracy of answers given at confidence 3; count of 🔥 | ≥ 90%, few 🔥 | Slow down; name the qualifiers before reading the options |
| **Independent check** | A mock after each domain, scored on taught objectives only | ≥ 80% on taught objectives, not falling | Style gap → more scenario practice; content gap → re-teach |
| **Reading slips** | Misses where the knowledge was right but a qualifier was missed, or the wrong letter was entered. Tally: (none yet) | Trending to 0 | Qualifier-first habit; answer as letter + 2-3 word reason |
| **Pace** | Sessions done vs the Daily schedule | On schedule or ahead | Merge light objectives; use the buffer |

